{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank","id":1025758,"title":"[2E] Ghosts & Integrity - How to get your Rank","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T23:52:31-08:00","id":1025758,"title":"[2E] Ghosts & Integrity - How to get your Rank","content":"So we have pointing out how becoming ghost after death is working in game by one of devs working on <b>Geist: Sin - Eaters</b> 2E. Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=999603#post999603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's generally tied to Integrity at the moment of death. There are occasional exceptions (and of course in-universe it's a little more ambiguous because people can't see their own character sheets), but the rule of thumb is if your Integrity is &lt; 7, you come back Rank 1, if it's 7-9 you come back Rank 2, and if it's 10 you don't leave a ghost at all; whether that means you just stop existing or go back into the wheel of reincarnation or skip the busted-ass Underworld altogether and pass on to the &quot;real&quot; afterlife is anybody's guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm weird, but did not the progression should be in reverse? High Integrity, less disturbed host you become? Rank 2 ghosts are to be run as almost dedicated characters, going for almost Aspirations, from what I know about setting lore on them - and those will be much more low Integrity than 'almost saints ones'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T00:00:56-08:00","id":1025762,"title":"","content":"So now instead of torturing people to death to grind their Integrity and create a Ghost that I can mine for data and secrets, I need to patch up their Integrity but not too much? That will lead to some wacky Mage protocols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:14:47-08:00","id":1025769,"title":"","content":"I think I would be much more okay with this progression:<br /> <br /> Integrity: 7-10 -&gt; You go to the Afterlife, not living the ghost behind you.<br /> Integrity: 6-5 -&gt; You leave Rank 1 ghost.<br /> Integrity: 4 and lower -&gt; You leave Rank 2 ghost.<br /> <br /> From the lore of 1E ghosts are left when something <i>bad </i>happen to you. Not every person leave one - most even don't. And those higher in Rank are 'more mad' and seperated from humanity. As most humanity work to have higher than lower Integrity, it works with with setting as we have it. Also, we need this for the scenes like this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://horrorfilmcentral.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/ps_shot3l.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:20:35-08:00","id":1025772,"title":"","content":"Rank 2 ghosts are more &quot;human&quot; than rank 1 ghosts in 2e, so it makes sense for the people with more stable souls to coalesce into the more human ghosts rather than crazed echoes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And those higher in Rank are 'more mad' and seperated from humanity. </div> </div> </div>That is only for ghosts warped by the underworld. So Rank 3+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:33:26-08:00","id":1025775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025772#post1025772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 2 ghosts are more &quot;human&quot; than rank 1 ghosts in 2e, so it makes sense for the people with more stable souls to coalesce into the more human ghosts rather than crazed echoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for 2E it should be then something like this:<br /> Integrity 7-10 -&gt; You go to the Afterlife, not living the ghost behind you.<br /> Integrity 6-5 -&gt; You leave Rank 2 ghost.<br /> Integrity 4 and lower -&gt; You leave Rank 1 ghost.<br /> <br /> Most people should not leave ghost or we will have 'over population' of Twilight. Most of humanity has Integrity 7, so it does have sense to limit this and any above Integrity from ghost creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:38:55-08:00","id":1025778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025775#post1025775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people should not leave ghost or we will have 'over population' of Twilight. Most of humanity has Integrity 7, so it does have sense to limit this and any above Integrity from ghost creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't suggesting everyone comes back as a ghost except for people with 10 integrity, he was saying why some ghosts come into the world at different ranks. They still need a &quot;something&quot; to come back as a ghost in the first place before integrity determines their rank (and if the person is integrity ten, then they don't make a ghost even if something happens that would make them a ghost).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:45:16-08:00","id":1025780,"title":"","content":"High-Ranking ghosts aren't those gone mad. They're those that became more cognizant. Rank 1 ghosts are psychic recordings who aren't even aware of what they are. Rank 2 ghosts realize that they're dead people. Go Rank 3 and beyond, and ghosts slowly understand that they're not the same person as the dead one, and that they're not human anymore, and start to reach out to their true potential as nascent death-gods.<br /> <br /> A Rank 1 ghost can only haunt its site of death, replaying its last moments of life or death. They can't go on a quest for vengeance, because they don't even know they need one. A Rank 2 ghost, on the other hand, is very aware of how it died, and is likely out for blood. The latter rising from people who are (relatively) more self-aware, represented by high Integrity, seems to make sense for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:50:26-08:00","id":1025782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025778#post1025778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He wasn't suggesting everyone comes back as a ghost except for people with 10 integrity, he was saying why some ghosts come into the world at different ranks. They still need a &quot;something&quot; to come back as a ghost in the first place before integrity determines their rank (and if the person is integrity ten, then they don't make a ghost even if something happens that would make them a ghost).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does have transfer on other gamelines, like for example <b>Mage</b> and it's ghosts population. And like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> mentioned - creating ghost from your prisoner <i>should</i> be viable tactics.<br /> <br /> Even then if we assume <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> proposed spread of ghosts - we get <b>more</b> Rank 2 ghosts than Rank 1. Simply because of most humanity is having Integrity 7. If both Rank 1 and Rank 2 need same 'something' to come back ( I assume Anchor or special Aspiration in the moment of death ), the only difference in populations is Integrity levels. And most humans has Integrity 7 ( more or less ) in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> universe.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, high Integrity characters are too rare to make them needed for Rank 2 ghosts - finding one in most chronicles is tough. And Rank 2 ghosts are more numerous than those. But still their numbers should be <b>much</b> lower than Rank 1 ghosts.<br /> <br /> So we end with non sense Integrity progression or overpopulation of Twilight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T02:06:42-08:00","id":1025788,"title":"","content":"Well, what's wrong with more ghosts being self-aware? They've been always the more populous type of ephemeral entity in the physical world. Them being at least being able to talk to mediums looks nice to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T02:14:27-08:00","id":1025790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025788#post1025788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what's wrong with more ghosts being self-aware? They've been always the more populous type of ephemeral entity in the physical world. Them being at least being able to talk to mediums looks nice to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's contrary to gamelines canon. Here is quote from <b>CoD Ruleboo</b>k:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p.122</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ranging from broken, animated afterimages, unable to do anything but reenact their death, to intelligent, malevolent, once-human spirits with power over whatever kind of calamity killed them, the world teems with vast numbers of the restless dead. <b>More ghosts exist than any other supernatural creature, but the truly powerful, independent specters of legend are rare.</b><br /> <b>The majority of ghosts are poor at influencing the world, trapped in their insubstantial state and unable to even Manifest, noticed only as a strange chill or eerie vibe if the living sense them at all. </b>Ghosts are drawn to places and people that they had emotional connections to in life \u2014 these anchor the ghost in the world and allow those with enough power to Manifest, whereupon they carry out whatever mad urges they still feel and attempt, in their broken state, to further the goals they left undone in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 1 ghosts should have much higher numbers than Rank 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T02:30:27-08:00","id":1025793,"title":"","content":"I don't see any part of the lines you bolded saying anything about the self-awareness of ghosts. Only their impotency.<br /> <br /> I see the &quot;truly powerful, independent specters of legend&quot; that are rare as the Rank 3+ ones. They're rare because they're stuck in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> And &quot;The majority of ghosts are poor at influencing the world&quot; because they're only at Rank 1-2. Even at Rank 2, there's only so much an ephemeral entity can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T02:54:36-08:00","id":1025796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025790#post1025790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">creating ghost from your prisoner <i>should</i> be viable tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is as much as it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we end with non sense Integrity progression or overpopulation of Twilight </div> </div> </div>I still don't see how the integrity progression is non-sensical, more stable souls lead to more stable ghosts. Simple. And the overpopulation doesn't happen because things need to happen for a ghost to be made, like a person who dies distressed and alone, a crazed murderer, or a overpowering desire to keep their child safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rank 1 ghosts should have much higher numbers than Rank 2. </div> </div> </div>And that's what happens, because the circumstances which cause the creation of ghosts tends to occur more to individuals with low integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:01:06-08:00","id":1025801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025796#post1025796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is as much as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it does not. Being locked up in prison ( or just cuffed ) wold be small Breaking Point for most persons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025796#post1025796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see how the integrity progression is non-sensical, more stable souls lead to more stable ghosts. Simple. And the overpopulation doesn't happen because things need to happen for a ghost to be made, like a person who dies distressed and alone, a crazed murderer, or a overpowering desire to keep their child safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things happen to both high and low Integrity people - just low Integrity ones have more events like those in their lives. But in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, <i>anyone</i> (can) die with those motives. Murders are higher rating, missing persons are higher - heck, it's said in canon that anyone <i>alive</i> has been 'touched' by supernatural. If all that is to make ghost is 'I need some unfinished business' than like 80% of world population that die right now will become ghosts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025796#post1025796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's what happens, because the circumstances which cause the creation of ghosts tends to occur more to individuals with low integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>More to low Integrity, but almost anyone in CoD universe can become ghost by having one of those reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:06:10-08:00","id":1025802,"title":"","content":"This is kinda getting close to the &quot;What's the ratio of (given supernatural type) in a city's population&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And not in a good way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:13:34-08:00","id":1025807,"title":"","content":"That's what happens when you state things like this without thinking about their consequences for the ecology. Then again, I won't state my opinion on this, because I didn't read the whole thing and I'm basing my comments only on the stuff from the first post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:16:02-08:00","id":1025808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025802#post1025802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kinda getting close to the &quot;What's the ratio of (given supernatural type) in a city's population&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And not in a good way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it should, because those rules imply number of ghosts in setting, they general spread and from who they are made. VERY important informations for Death Arcanum having mages, for example.<br /> <br /> We know that spirits, on the other hand, are almost everywhere and connected to high Resonant places. So we can easily imagine their 'population spread' over setting.<br /> <br /> With proposed guidelines fro ghosts, it would look like there are almost only Rank 1 ghosts in Twilight, one on the 100 or so Rank 2 - and that's it. I always assumed Rank 2 ghosts are much more often than those rules imply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:39:10-08:00","id":1025820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025808#post1025808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it should, because those rules imply number of ghosts in setting, they general spread and from who they are made. VERY important informations for Death Arcanum having mages, for example.<br /> <br /> We know that spirits, on the other hand, are almost everywhere and connected to high Resonant places. So we can easily imagine their 'population spread' over setting.<br /> <br /> With proposed guidelines fro ghosts, it would look like there are almost only Rank 1 ghosts in Twilight, one on the 100 or so Rank 2 - and that's it. I always assumed Rank 2 ghosts are much more often than those rules imply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike Spirit mages, who get left behind without enough spirits to go around, Death mages have plenty of other things to do even without ghosts. And even if most ghosts are Rank 1 and of limited use to mages, Death mages can still boost their Rank to make them useful.<br /> <br /> And for the purposes of determining the ghost population, let's assume the combined number of Rank 1 and 2 ghosts are stable (since Integrity 10 people are indeed going to be rare). Then, the variable factor that decides whether Rank 1 ghosts are more populous or Rank 2 ones are is the average Integrity of humans in the setting.<br /> <br /> You assume Rank 1 ghosts will be the majority with the paramters GimpInBlack put up. This means that you are assuming most people who do leave ghosts do so at Integrity 1-6. This, in turn, means that you are assuming people who suffer Integrity loss do not put extra effort at all into reconstructing their shaken sense of perspective with introspection and therapy (represented in-game by spending Experiences to buy back Integrity)<br /> <br /> Between the large number of people who die at Integrity 1-6, and a sizeable number of people among them who do take effort to build up their Integrity back to 7-9, I don't think the ratio of Rank 1 and 2 ghosts will be that skewed.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry if all the &quot;You assume&quot; parts sounds aggressive or confrontational. It kinda sounds so after proof-reading what I wrote. I didn't mean it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-03-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:54:24-08:00","id":1025827,"title":"","content":"I wish Death had less focus on playing Pokemon GhOst and focused it's attention elsewhere, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:00:23-08:00","id":1025831,"title":"","content":"Considering that Integrity 10 people don't leave ghosts at all I think it would be reasonable if lower Integrity increases the chance of a ghost left behind. That alone can explain why Rank 1 ghosts are more common, if one's interpretation is that they should be more common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:21:07-08:00","id":1025841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025820#post1025820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Sorry if all the &quot;You assume&quot; parts sounds aggressive or confrontational. It kinda sounds so after proof-reading what I wrote. I didn't mean it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay, we are making debate here, some statement are to be seen. But let's look over this problem in detail...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025820#post1025820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the large number of people who die at Integrity 1-6, and a sizeable number of people among them who do take effort to build up their Integrity back to 7-9, I don't think the ratio of Rank 1 and 2 ghosts will be that skewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made mistake making previous claim that they not return to higher Integrity. But the game practice most characters are in Integrity 7-6 territory - after 12 years of running <b>CoD</b> games I did not seen anyone character with Mortality/Integrity 8+ , non of my few dozens of players. I did seen once or twice in derived traits ( Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, etc. ) but almost never for mortals characters. So I make claim from practice running that Integrity 8+ characters are <i>very</i> rare.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Integrity 7 mortals is like 80% of worlds populations in First World, trying to be reasonable stable, denying supernatural all day long. Integrity 6 is like rest 18% of population that has some life problems ( and most try to return to Integrity 7 level ), from time to time, with only maybe 2% of rest possible Integrity levels.<br /> <br /> Now, let's look on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> guidelines compared to <b>CoD</b> universe population:<br /> <br /> Integrity 7 - About 80% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 6 and less - About 19% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 1 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 8-9 - Less than 1% of mortal population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts ( if any will be )<br /> <br /> It suddenly make Rank 2 ghosts most populate supernatural entirety in <b>CoD</b> universe, four times more populous thatn Rank 1 ghosts. But books to this day states it's Rank 1 rather. ( Also Rank 2 ghosts are harder to run, as they need to be <i>much</i> more fleshed out. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:27:45-08:00","id":1025842,"title":"","content":"The problem is that if you even goes with basic Gimp's guidelines, but change that Integrity 7 also makes Rank 1 ghosts ( that restores populations sizes to those shown by books to this time, more or less ), then we end with like 1-2% of populations only becoming Rank 2 ghosts on death - that seems too low.<br /> <br /> Not too mention that Rank 2 seemed to be to be those all 'vengeful ghosts' from popculture, and as such should have low Integrity, in first place. You do not make ghost story about Rank 1 ghosts vengeance on living, rather Rank 2 ones, don't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:34:04-08:00","id":1025846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025841#post1025841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made mistake making previous claim that they not return to higher Integrity. But the game practice most characters are in Integrity 7-6 territory - after 12 years of running <b>CoD</b> games I did not seen anyone character with Mortality/Integrity 8+ , non of my few dozens of players. I did seen once or twice in derived traits ( Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, etc. ) but almost never for mortals characters. So I make claim from practice running that Integrity 8+ characters are <i>very</i> rare.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Integrity 7 mortals is like 80% of worlds populations in First World, trying to be reasonable stable, denying supernatural all day long. Integrity 6 is like rest 18% of population that has some life problems, from time to time, with only maybe 2% of rest possible Integrity levels.<br /> <br /> Now, let's look on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> guidlines compared to CoD universe population:<br /> <br /> Integrity 7 - About 80% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 6 and less - About 19% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 1 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 8-9 - Less than 1% of mortal population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts.<br /> <br /> It suddenly make Rank 2 ghosts most populate supernatural entiety in <b>CoD</b> universe. But books states it's Rank 1 rather.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Player characters have little incentive to raise Integrity, unless they're mortal exorcists. But the various mortal NPCs in tthe setting probably will, seeing how they won't be spending as much as Exp on Attributes, Skills, Merits and powers like PCs will. So that's where the Rank 2 ghosts would come from - those who build up/back their Integrity. But at the same time, people who don't properly recover after trauma are a dime a dozen, so that's where the Rank 1 ghosts would come from.<br /> <br /> So it seems I'm in agreement with you in assessing that there will be a lot of Rank 2 ghosts out there. But in disagreement over just how much they would be - I'm seeing the rate of high-Integrity mortals and mid-to-low-Integrity mortals about the same. Now I'm curious - where did you get that estimate percentage on Integrity? I don't think that many people would keep Integrity 7 on ghost-generating circumstances, which will most likely include trauma one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:43:22-08:00","id":1025849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025842#post1025842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that if you even goes with basic Gimp's guidelines, but change that Integrity 7 also makes Rank 1 ghosts ( that restores populations sizes to those shown by books to this time, more or less ), then we end with like 1-2% of populations only becoming Rank 2 ghosts on death - that seems too low.<br /> <br /> Not too mention that Rank 2 seemed to be to be those all 'vengeful ghosts' from popculture, and as such should have low Integrity, in first place. You do not make ghost story about Rank 1 ghosts vengeance on living, rather Rank 2 ones, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first sentence I've just replied to in the previous post.<br /> <br /> The second sentence, well, why would being vengeful equal not having a clearer sense of self and a firmer perspective on the world (represented by low Integrity)? Integrity 10 characters are basically so calm and resolute, even when facing their death, that they have no regrets. Closest thing to enlightenment, as far as I can tell. Integrity 7-9 characters aren't that enlightened, but what they are is determined. Determined to persist after death and kick the ass of whoever the hell it is that did them in. Below that you have people who are so much in (spiritual) pain that they can't muster the will to face their deaths, and continue to deny them - hence the self-repeating behavior of Rank 1 ghosts.<br /> <br /> Ghost stories featuring Rank 1 ghosts are those typical ones on haunted houses and ghost spots. In fact, where I come from, most ghosts in most ghost stories don't have much of a personality, and just haunt the living for sake of haunting. Maybe this is why I have an easier time accepting that Rank 1 ghosts are the majority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:43:56-08:00","id":1025850,"title":"","content":"One thing I find weird about this that most of &quot;iconic&quot; strong Ghosts - murderers, revenge driven people, obsessive lovers etc - don't feel like Integrity 7 material to me. Then again, I'm not Geist target market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:53:21-08:00","id":1025854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025850#post1025850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I find weird about this that most of &quot;iconic&quot; strong Ghosts - murderers, revenge driven people, obsessive lovers etc - don't feel like Integrity 7 material to me. Then again, I'm not Geist target market.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already said it in the post just a split second before this one, but my interpretation is that high Integrity for ghosts stand in for the determination to persist after death. Traumatized individuals prefer to just let the pain go away, seeing death as an escape, and lock themselves in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:05:25-08:00","id":1025859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025854#post1025854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already said it in the post just a split second before this one, but my interpretation is that high Integrity for ghosts stand in for the determination to persist after death. Traumatized individuals prefer to just let the pain go away, seeing death as an escape, and lock themselves in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, continuing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> thought, that this goes against established rules of Integrity <b>and </b>ghosts. From <b>CoD Rulebook</b> quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alone among ephemeral beings, ghosts also possess Integrity, set at the level they had before death. Their Integrity scores don\u2019t change, however, as ghosts do not suffer breaking points. Their self-image is fixed, unless something happens to push them back to the level of cognizance and self-awareness they had in life. If this should happen somehow, they can suffer breaking points the same way living people can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our typical 'ghost story villain' are murderers, revenge driven people, obsessive lovers - and those people most probable will <b>not </b>have Integrity 7+ on their death - rather Integrity 6 and lower. And even <i>percent</i> of them will be doing what they were doing <b>and</b> have Integrity 8 or more in the moment of death. That means we very have strong dissonance her between presented guidelines and rest of <b>CoD </b>mechanics and canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:17:56-08:00","id":1025862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025859#post1025859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is, continuing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> thought, that this goes against established rules of Integrity <b>and </b>ghosts. From <b>CoD Rulebook</b> quote:<br /> <br /> Our typical 'ghost story villain' are murderers, revenge driven people, obsessive lovers - and those people most probable will <b>not </b>have Integrity 7+ on their death - rather Integrity 6 and lower. And even <i>percent</i> of them will be doing what they were doing <b>and</b> have Integrity 8 or more in the moment of death. That means we very have strong dissonance her between presented guidelines and rest of <b>CoD </b>mechanics and canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the part you quote says, Integrity represents self-image and self-awareness. Which I find necessary to pursue objectives centered on the self, such as vengeance and love.<br /> <br /> Would someone whose sense of self has been broken by hardships and worn out by life <i>want </i>to cling on to the things that most likely made them miserable in the first place? They might, but only after patching back themselves up together and clearly recognizing the source of their miseries - represented by raising back Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:52:43-08:00","id":1025871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025841#post1025841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, let's look on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> guidelines compared to <b>CoD</b> universe population:<br /> <br /> Integrity 7 - About 80% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 6 and less - About 19% of mortals population -&gt; Instant Rank 1 ghosts ( if any will be ).<br /> Integrity 8-9 - Less than 1% of mortal population -&gt; Instant Rank 2 ghosts ( if any will be )<br /> <br /> It suddenly make Rank 2 ghosts most populate supernatural entirety in <b>CoD</b> universe, four times more populous thatn Rank 1 ghosts. But books to this day states it's Rank 1 rather. ( Also Rank 2 ghosts are harder to run, as they need to be <i>much</i> more fleshed out. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Since most people don't come back as ghosts. It needs something severe or special to leave such an echo. Things like that happening throughout someones life generally leads to them having lower integrity and thus, most ghosts will probably come from people with low integrity.<br /> <br /> Ghosts only exist when it makes sense for them to come into existence, 98% of people don't leave ghosts to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:42:47-08:00","id":1025900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025862#post1025862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the part you quote says, Integrity represents self-image and self-awareness. Which I find necessary to pursue objectives centered on the self, such as vengeance and love.<br /> <br /> Would someone whose sense of self has been broken by hardships and worn out by life <i>want </i>to cling on to the things that most likely made them miserable in the first place? They might, but only after patching back themselves up together and clearly recognizing the source of their miseries - represented by raising back Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patch and raising is going back to Integrity 7 area - and not even this mean they <i>should</i> be precisely 7 at scale to work and live more or less. By actions of typical 'ghost story villain' they will plunge down in to Integrity from level of 7, maybe to like 4-5. Then they will try to re-establish themselves, so they go to Integrity about 6 - it's enough to go on in normal life, more or less, but it's also leave you place to return to your obsession that lead you astray in the first place. Until you are becoming shaman/exorcist, nothing in Integrity rules marks you to go up to 8 or even 7 for that matter. After becoming murderer or having heavy trauma experience, there is no need to become saint, rules wise.<b> You just want to return to 'rather normal' - and many times it's just Integrity 6. And this is why most character will <i>never</i> be Integrity 8 mortals in the first place.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:52:19-08:00","id":1025908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025871#post1025871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Since most people don't come back as ghosts. It needs something severe or special to leave such an echo. Things like that happening throughout someones life generally leads to them having lower integrity and thus, most ghosts will probably come from people with low integrity.<br /> <br /> Ghosts only exist when it makes sense for them to come into existence, 98% of people don't leave ghosts to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are sure? Because in CoD everyday sounds like ghosts creation event - violent accidents, killed by murderer, lost in the woods ( never to be found ), and a like. Not to adding all those tragically loved, manipulated by various supernaturals in killing themselves or losing their loved ones, weird disease and many, many, 'not peaceful' reasons.<br /> <br /> I do not say that everybody in CoD dies in the way that will bring back ghost - but much, <b>much </b>more people will. If in reality it would, let's say, about 0,1% population would create ghosts ( if they would be real ), then in CoD, by various forces and reasons I only shown small part of, it goes up to even 2% - and I would not be surprised to see even 5% of general population, on mass, in particular places.<br /> <br /> Most of them would have Integrity 7 in the moment of their death - as they would have only brush with 'troubles' or supernatural - but whatever future Anchor it is, is clinging them. It means A LOT of Rank 2 ghosts over Rank 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:58:59-08:00","id":1025917,"title":"","content":"Basically, my biggest crude with those guidelines is this - Rank 2 ghosts should be more violent and low Integrity, Rank 1 ghosts should be more stable - to make the typical 'ghost stories' more probable. Because now, with those guidelines, it looks like you almost do not get <i>any</i> violent Rank 2 ghosts - and those that <i>should</i> be violent are only 'will-o-whisps' and cold spots Rank 1. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:07:40-08:00","id":1025923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025900#post1025900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Patch and raising is going back to Integrity 7 area - and not even this mean they <i>should</i> be precisely 7 at scale to work and live more or less. By actions of typical 'ghost story villain' they will plunge down in to Integrity from level of 7, maybe to like 4-5. Then they will try to re-establish themselves, so they go to Integrity about 6 - it's enough to go on in normal life, more or less, but it's also leave you place to return to your obsession that lead you astray in the first place. Until you are becoming shaman/exorcist, nothing in Integrity rules marks you to go up to 8 or even 7 for that matter. After becoming murderer or having heavy trauma experience, there is no need to become saint, rules wise.<b> You just want to return to 'rather normal' - and many times it's just Integrity 6. And this is why most character will <i>never</i> be Integrity 8 mortals in the first place.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Integrity 6 be the point where the ghost-to-be person reestablishes himself but still keeps his obsessions? Why not 7, 8, or 9? I say with certainty that Integrity 10 is the only point where one wouldn't have any regrets or obsessions left, but only because it's literally the maximum point. Any point below is still grounds for character flaws.<br /> <br /> Raising your Integrity isn't about becoming a saint. That has connotations of morality and/or ethics. It's reaffirming your strength of character and force of personality. A murderer may justify his actions, or develop a twisted sense of self-righteousness. In fact, isn't that how murderers who don't confess or commit suicide out of guilt work? They justify themselves. That's what raising Integrity represents, not redeeming yourself.<br /> <br /> Integrity is not about being moral, or ethical. It never was. It is about being a person, a human being. And humans can be so many beings, unrepenting murderers and obsessive lovers included. &quot;Villainaous ghosts should have low Integrity&quot; will be true if Integrity is about being moral, ethical, or sane by contemporary societal standards. But it's not. You can have a stable psyche and still be a villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:13:50-08:00","id":1025925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025917#post1025917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, my biggest crude with those guidelines is this - Rank 2 ghosts should be more violent and low Integrity, Rank 1 ghosts should be more stable - to make the typical 'ghost stories' more probable. Because now, with those guidelines, it looks like you almost do not get <i>any</i> violent Rank 2 ghosts - and those that <i>should</i> be violent are only 'will-o-whisps' and cold spots Rank 1. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Our posts crossed times once again, so I reiterate:<br /> <br /> 1) Being violent (or criminal, or vicious, or villainous) does not always mean that the guy has a flawed and shaken sense of self. Rank 2 ghosts, spawned from a relatively more stable psyche, can certainly be malevolent, because there are plenty of people who are malevolent despite having a stable psyche.<br /> <br /> 2) There are just as many ghost stories where the ghost is not a &quot;person&quot; that interacts with the living, but a &quot;thing&quot; that lashes out at people for some reason the livings only suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:33:37-08:00","id":1025935,"title":"","content":"I guess the biggest problem is the fact that Rank is also directly tied to the power of the ghost in question, with the weakest Rank 2 Ghost being stronger than Strongest Rank 1 Ghost. <br /> Again, your ghostly villain won't be a much of a villain if he barely can do anything in comparison to a kind ghost who was a pretty ok person and for some reason is twice as powerful as the violent crazy murder ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:48:36-08:00","id":1025938,"title":"","content":"Really, you cannot have good 'murderous ghost' as it need high Integrity in the first place - being murderer by life, does not make good things on your Integrity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025923#post1025923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Integrity 6 be the point where the ghost-to-be person reestablishes himself but still keeps his obsessions? Why not 7, 8, or 9? I say with certainty that Integrity 10 is the only point where one wouldn't have any regrets or obsessions left, but only because it's literally the maximum point. Any point below is still grounds for character flaws.<br /> <br /> Raising your Integrity isn't about becoming a saint. That has connotations of morality and/or ethics. It's reaffirming your strength of character and force of personality. A murderer may justify his actions, or develop a twisted sense of self-righteousness. In fact, isn't that how murderers who don't confess or commit suicide out of guilt work? They justify themselves. That's what raising Integrity represents, not redeeming yourself.<br /> <br /> Integrity is not about being moral, or ethical. It never was. It is about being a person, a human being. And humans can be so many beings, unrepenting murderers and obsessive lovers included. &quot;Villainous ghosts should have low Integrity&quot; will be true if Integrity is about being moral, ethical, or sane by contemporary societal standards. But it's not. You can have a stable psyche and still be a villain.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>WHY would character rose his Integrity above level of 7, after commiting murders or having great trauma? </b>Only reason I can see for being Integrity 8+ character is to have bonus on abjuration, i.e. being 'exorcists/shaman'. Like I written before - to this day I did not seen <i>any</i> high Integrity character that was not trying to be 'saint' in the first place. And yes, I know Integrity is supposed to not be about ethics - but it still is, if it goes down if you kill people. Just from math point of view.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you sure will not high Integrity murderer. He may bounce in and out of Integrity 7 level, but there is <i>nothing</i> for him to have Integrity 8+, in reality. Bonus +1 to roll to resist Breaking Points for commiting crimes is just not worth of XP investment - much better is buying Merit, like <i>Meditative Mind</i>. This and standard for mortal characters to have Integrity 7 means our murderer-to-be-ghost will very unlikely have Integrity 8+ and by this - <b>those guidelines on making 'high Integrity Rank 2 killer' are not working with the rules of Integrity as written.</b> And by this whole Rank guidelines not working with CoD mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:51:06-08:00","id":1025940,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with 21C here. People seem to be mistakenly equating Integrity to some form of morality. Just because you have a high Integrity (and thus high Rank) doesn't mean you're &quot;kind.&quot; Low Integrity can be kind. High Integrity can be vicious, mean and revenge-driven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:54:55-08:00","id":1025941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025940#post1025940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with 21C here. People seem to be mistakenly equating Integrity to some form of morality. Just because you have a high Integrity (and thus high Rank) doesn't mean you're &quot;kind.&quot; Low Integrity can be kind. High Integrity can be vicious, mean and revenge-driven.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still does not see High Integrity 'vicious, mean and revenge-driven' characters - they just not 'poping up' with mechanics as they are written in 2E CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:12:21-08:00","id":1025946,"title":"","content":"Things I don't see people taking into account:<br /> <br /> 1) It is implied that almost EVERYONE leaves a ghost back in the Underworld. Integrity 10 people seem to be the exception. I don't see those guidelines reflecting on the Ghost population on Twilight, but rather the Underworld's.<br /> 2) Most murderers have only killed once. So even if killing is always a breaking point, it doesn't mean that their Integrity would be in shambles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:20:14-08:00","id":1025950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025946#post1025946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It is implied that almost EVERYONE leaves a ghost back in the Underworld. Integrity 10 people seem to be the exception. I don't see those guidelines reflecting on the Ghost population on Twilight, but rather the Underworld's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not seen this anywhere - could you point or cite source on this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025946#post1025946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Most murderers have only killed once. So even if killing is always a breaking point, it doesn't mean that their Integrity would be in shambles.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not talk about 'most people' here. We talk about 'ghost story' movie trope of local murderer ( possible killing at least few people ) and that by the now guidelines he will be much weaker ghost than 'good doing, law abiding' normal persons. Which is totally inverses from almost all known popculture I know ( and most <b>CoD</b> is based on popculture tropes ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:23:42-08:00","id":1025951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025938#post1025938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, you cannot have good 'murderous ghost' as it need high Integrity in the first place - being murderer by life, does not make good things on your Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div> You are mistaken on several counts. First of all, you can have a murderer with high Integrity - most murderer don't go out and kill repeatedly in short amount of time. In fact, most killers only murder someone that's committed a deeply personal offense, and that's very rare. Secondly, you aren't touching on the idea that the murderer can pass the breaking point check. Its not an automatic loss, and there are ways to boost the dice pool.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument hinges on the idea of murder ghost must be a mass murderer or something similar. And that murder must absolutely be a breaking point. Breaking points are highly subjective, and the guidelines we have are deliberately open to debate. The book is merely giving suggestions, with repeated insistances to take individual experiences, upbringing and moral frameworks into account.<br /> <br /> You keep pushing the idea of Integrity as Morality. You are highly insistant upon it. You want to run things that way, go for it. That's not what Integrity is meant to measure, and insisting upon that it does does not make it objectively true for all. You want to run it that way? More power to you. But you cannot insist that everyone must run it your way.<br /> <br /> <b>WHY would character rose his Integrity about level of 7, after commiting murders or having great trauma? </b>[/quote] Why wouldn't they? That's entirely your assumption that people won't raise Integrity (or equivalents). Players tend to ignore it, because of XP costs, but your average NPC doesn't track experience costs. Instead, they happily reaffirm their sense of self by hanging out with friends and family, going to work, and so on. Living a normal, every day life. And that results in raising Integrity.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> And here's a part that is being ignored. Even if you claim that its impossible for a murderer to have a Rank 2 ghost upon death... then let it be a Rank 1, fall into the Underworld, and escape as a Rank 3 or higher ghost. Rare is not the same thing as never happening. Tada, super powerful murder-ghost. Alternatively, Inferno whisperers can still infect a murder-ghost and raise their Rank. Maybe a necromancer (pick any game line, even mortal psychic) did it. Also, lets not forget that Rank 1 ghosts can still kill someone if they try.<br /> <br /> There's lots of ways to run this. And, lets be perfectly honest, if you find the cannon method is interfering with your game? <i>Then change it to fit your game</i>. No need to argue about it. You obviously have different assumptions at your table than the writers developers are using. Certainly, you are saying things that I think are fine at your table, but will never fit at mine or any number of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025941#post1025941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still does not see High Integrity 'vicious, mean and revenge-driven' characters - they just not 'poping up' with mechanics as they are written in 2E CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see vicious mean or revenge driven characters with High Integrity? I do. There is absolutely NOTHING about such a character that hits breaking points if the ST says it doesn't. Its not supernatural, its not violating a personal code or society at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-03-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:28:12-08:00","id":1025954,"title":"","content":"Most ghosts in ghost stories are victims, not murderers.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a little early to be complaining about a concept of a game when the game doesn't exist yet and your problem stems from a post taken out of context during the development process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-03-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:36:16-08:00","id":1025959,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Even most murderer ghosts became murderers AFTER their death, in order to commit revenge against a crime or injustice they were victims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:56:34-08:00","id":1025965,"title":"","content":"Okay, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, let's assume you are right and many characters can have Integrity 7+ while committing grievous crimes. This leads us that most persons becoming ghost on Integrity 7 ( as those characters are most numerous worldwide ). And this leads us to Rank 2 overflooding Rank 1 ghosts - that by <b>CoD</b> canon should be reverse.<br /> <br /> Not too mention you cannot have Blood Merry-like ghosts that are avenging their life torturers - persons leaving those ghosts are having low Integrity just from getting many Breaking Points on physical or social violence.<br /> <br /> Simpler than making all those circumstances for 'stable person' to work with 'evil' or 'tortured' as ghost,<b> would be just to say that high Integrity ( like 7 or 6. till maybe 8 ) leave Rank 1 ghosts and those that have lower Integrity ( lower than 6 ) leave Rank 2 ghosts.</b> It takes nothing from rules as written, works with common lore of popculture and <b>CoD</b> books and makes both murderer ghosts and 'vengeful tortured ones' work perfectly with rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:59:49-08:00","id":1025968,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that ghosts can't raise their Rank outside the Underworld for the most part, and thus the higher baseline of cognizance afforded to a Rank 2 starter ghost serves to make people with solid self-images the basis for most convincingly personlike ghosts that stand a chance of resolving unfinished business cleanly.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 ghosts are more often rooted in raw passion and/or lack the wherewithal to act subtly, and thus will generally stick around until they're banished to the Underworld by exorcism or the ravages of time, whereupon they proceed to pick up the less genteel forms of self-awareness common to a place that inverts the Anchors of mortals and runneth over with nightmarish vistas.<br /> <br /> Ghosts you can talk to without engaging in minor blood sacrifice are rare if you're after one that hasn't been to the Underworld and eminently more human in their outlook. That's the whole point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:03:10-08:00","id":1025969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025954#post1025954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most ghosts in ghost stories are victims, not murderers.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025959#post1025959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Even most murderer ghosts became murderers AFTER their death, in order to commit revenge against a crime or injustice they were victims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Victims still get's Breaking Points on Integrity by being victims to violence. <b>Repeatedly. </b>So it's much more probable they will have lower Integrity than higher. With guidelines like those presented in opening post, it's looks like 'vengeful ghosts' should be not moved by the violence they were taken under in life. Which is disservice to whole concept of 'being tortured in life'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025954#post1025954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it's a little early to be complaining about a concept of a game when the game doesn't exist yet and your problem stems from a post taken out of context during the development process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those rules will affect whole <b>CoD</b> games universe, just like portray of Underworld in <b>Geist </b>1E was made canon and it's fundament for <b>Mage</b> 2E games now. <b>Development process is <i>exactly</i> moment you rise this kind concerns.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:07:43-08:00","id":1025971,"title":"","content":"I still think lower Integrity has a larger chance of leaving a ghost since Integrity 10 never leaves any. That solves the fact that Rank 1 ghosts are more numerous in the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:19:05-08:00","id":1025976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025969#post1025969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With guidelines like those presented in opening post, it's looks like 'vengeful ghosts' should be not moved by the violence they were taken under in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am a howling shade consumed by my desire for revenge, I do not need greater cognizance than necessary to spot an identifying feature and will not likely be satisfied by the mere bringing-to-justice of my murderer. I need <i>power</i>.<br /> <br /> And, my goodness, is it my fevered imagination or is that a massive pit of entropy clogged with the energies of grief and rage and Death Itself?<br /> <br /> You can keep my broken murder weapon \u2014 I'll be <i>right back</i>. Just need to get some stuff from Downstairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Misspelling. 01-03-2017, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:25:07-08:00","id":1025982,"title":"","content":"Was there ever any Ghost-Spirit crossover? This whole thread makes me think what could happen if a Ghost was so consumed by and definied by their desire for something, that their personality and identity would erode to the point where they are closer to a Spirit than a Ghost. <br /> I'm not keen on lines that focus on Ghosts / Spirit World, so was there ever anything like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:26:14-08:00","id":1025984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025976#post1025976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am a howling shade consumed by my desire for revenge, I do not need greater cognizance and will not likely be satisfied by the mere bringing-to-justice of my murderer. I need <i>power</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the <i>power</i> is given by having Rank 2 instead of Rank 1. Like, literally, you can have more dots in Power Attributes and more Numina. Higher Rank means power!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025976#post1025976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, my goodness, is it my fevered imagination or is that a massive pit of entropy clogged with the energies of grief and rage and Death Itself?<br /> <br /> You can keep my broken murder weapon \u2014 I'll be <i>right back</i>. Just need to get some stuff from Downstairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So any Rank 1 ghost can just do *poof* to go to Underworld, return from it with Rank 3 in the same day? ( I really do not know if it is possible ) Because if it's not, our 'vengeful tortured' ghost would not be interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:47:03-08:00","id":1025993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025965#post1025965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, let's assume you are right and many characters can have Integrity 7+ while committing grievous crimes. This leads us that most persons becoming ghost on Integrity 7 ( as those characters are most numerous worldwide ). And this leads us to Rank 2 overflooding Rank 1 ghosts - that by <b>CoD</b> canon should be reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div> First of all, you're the one who's insisting that it should be the reverse. There is no direct quote to back you up. I agree with the others that higher rank being rare refers to the Rank 3+ ghosts from the Underworld, not Rank 1 or Rank 2.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's no reason to assume that people who die with Integrity 7+ will become ghosts in equal or greater numbers than those of lower Integrity. The only information we have about Integrity relating to ghosts is that it affects Rank. We have no idea about anything else. Hells, we don't even know how ghosts of houses, animals or other non-human entities come about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not too mention you cannot have Blood Merry-like ghosts that are avenging their life torturers - persons leaving those ghosts are having low Integrity just from getting many Breaking Points on physical or social violence. </div> </div> </div> There are a ton of Bloody Mary legends, some even benevolant. You're going to have to be more specific. Even the antagonists from the movies named Bloody Mary are vastly different. <br /> <br /> Also, why are social / physical violence causing breaking points on these people? Where are the rules for that?<br /> <br /> And lastly, who says that a Rank 1 ghost can't go out and avenge their life's torturers? Rank 1 ghosts are still strong against mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simpler than making all those circumstances for 'stable person' to work with 'evil' or 'tortured' as ghost,<b> would be just to say that high Integrity ( like 7 or 6. till maybe 8 ) leave Rank 1 ghosts and those that have lower Integrity ( lower than 6 ) leave Rank 2 ghosts.</b> It takes nothing from rules as written, works with common lore of popculture and <b>CoD</b> books and makes both murderer ghosts and 'vengeful tortured ones' work perfectly with rules as written. </div> </div> </div>If you want to do that, sure. The problem I have is that your arguments are full of holes and you're insisting that your way is cannon. Its not, its just your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:59:48-08:00","id":1025998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025982#post1025982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there ever any Ghost-Spirit crossover? This whole thread makes me think what could happen if a Ghost was so consumed by and definied by their desire for something, that their personality and identity would erode to the point where they are closer to a Spirit than a Ghost.<br /> I'm not keen on lines that focus on Ghosts / Spirit World, so was there ever anything like this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a Giest. They have become emodiemients of their type of Death. In Giest 1E, they are affected by both the Death and Spirit Arcanum from mage and there is a sidebar with some theoretical origins that include them being actual spirit/ghost hybrids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:06:47-08:00","id":1026001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025984#post1025984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the <i>power</i> is given by having Rank 2 instead of Rank 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice that starting at Rank 2 means starting at a level of cognizance that recognizes not every red-haired man is their murderer and that it won't help to kill false positives, whereas starting at Rank 1 means the potentially-illusory promise of getting there <i>eventually</i> is reason enough for them to be an autonomous territorial serial killer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, literally, you can have more dots in Power Attributes and more Numina. Higher Rank means power! </div> </div> </div>Higher Rank is not mutually requisite of higher <i>starting</i> Rank and higher <i>starting</i> Rank generally comes with the good sense not to go poking around under the rock where the dead things live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So any Rank 1 ghost can just do *poof* to go to Underworld, return from it with Rank 3 in the same day? </div> </div> </div>Leave the goalposts where they were unless you have a vast library of ghost fiction whose central supernatural character fulfills their pursuit within the same day.<br /> <br /> My engaging in a half-meta description of the &quot;thought process&quot; that leads to a ghost with an obsession opting to stay in the Underworld to build their power for a while once banished there upon using the newfound awareness that Rank 2 provides is not a description of a conscious decision to leave its Anchor(s) behind \u2014 it's in keeping with the genre that the peace of the grave permits a fairly rapid return to one's faculties as a ghost who has lost its hold on the land of the living.<br /> <br /> Whether they're sufficiently desperate to go from there to drinking from one of the Rivers so soon is an academic question when the distinction I'm drawing is between types of Rank 2 ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because if it's not, our 'vengeful tortured' ghost would not be interested. </div> </div> </div>A Rank 1 ghost is accustomed to trying the same thing over and over and likely does not care about collateral damage. That's a combination of impulsive and obsessive that doesn't really lock out &quot;when given the choice between sharpening your ghost-knife before fighting your way back to the world you were cast down from and simply rushing the gates to try and get one last hit on your murderer, the former has narrative weight and precedent, while the latter is a dramatic image and occasionally a last-ditch exit hazard.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:11:23-08:00","id":1026006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First of all, you're the one who's insisting that it should be the reverse. There is no direct quote to back you up. I agree with the others that higher rank being rare refers to the Rank 3+ ghosts from the Underworld, not Rank 1 or Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot say how much you must miss reading <b>CoD corebook</b> to assume that Rank 2 should be more numerous:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 122</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of ghosts are poor at influencing the world, trapped in their insubstantial state and unable to even Manifest, noticed only as a strange chill or eerie vibe if the living sense them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 2 ghosts CAN Manifest, so this sentance must mean Rank 1 beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Secondly, there's no reason to assume that people who die with Integrity 7+ will become ghosts in equal or greater numbers than those of lower Integrity. The only information we have about Integrity relating to ghosts is that it affects Rank. We have no idea about anything else. Hells, we don't even know how ghosts of houses, animals or other non-human entities come about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just by sheer numbers - Integrity 7 is norm in mortal society. Rarely there are people with lower Integrity, so most dying people fulfilling 'ghosts needs' will be Integrity 7, it's simply statistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a ton of Bloody Mary legends, some even benevolant. You're going to have to be more specific. Even the antagonists from the movies named Bloody Mary are vastly different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant 'vengeful torture victim', like, you know, many of 'they were tortured by life and now are after her oppressors or their decedents'. This kind persons are having rather lower Integrity - and should be rather more cognitive than simple 'will-o-wisps' Rank 1 ghosts are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why are social / physical violence causing breaking points on these people? Where are the rules for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just see over Intimidation use on Violent Skills from <b>Hurt Locker</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hurt Locker, p.68</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, torture is the process of breaking down a person\u2019s Integrity systematically by subjecting them to breaking points in a controlled situation. It\u2019s similar to the rules in Empathy, above, except that a torturer is unlikely to stop at the point where the Broken Condition is applied. Further trauma might inflict Conditions such as Amnesia, Fugue, Madness, or whatever other Conditions may be appropriate. Healing these wounds, if they ever do really heal, will take years of therapy at minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Torture is <i>literally</i> treated as series Breaking Points to break Integrity. So torture victims have low Integrity by definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly, who says that a Rank 1 ghost can't go out and avenge their life's torturers? Rank 1 ghosts are still strong against mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>CoD Rulebook</b> says, simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 128</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsapient \u201crecording\u201d-type ghosts are Rank 1, while those that retain most of their living memories are Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Recording' types do not plan or avenge their murdered, they just repeat scene of their death, at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025993#post1025993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to do that, sure. The problem I have is that your arguments are full of holes and you're insisting that your way is cannon. Its not, its just your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see rather your augmentations as full of holes and trying to stretch things to work with 'devs initial idea'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:20:35-08:00","id":1026012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025969#post1025969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victims still get's Breaking Points on Integrity by being victims to violence. <b>Repeatedly. </b>So it's much more probable they will have lower Integrity than higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies they're repeated victims of abuse. A victim of murder doesn't get any Breaking Point. The victims of a car accident, gas leak, any of the normal 'sudden death' scenarios that fill out causes of ghosts in ghost stories wouldn't cause the problem. They're problematic ghosts because they don't realize they're dead. They try to go about their routine and it doesn't work and they grow frustrated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With guidelines like those presented in opening post, it's looks like 'vengeful ghosts' should be not moved by the violence they were taken under in life. Which is disservice to whole concept of 'being tortured in life'. </div> </div> </div>For one, you're taking things out of context. Two, victims of some sort of torturer and a torturer-killer are just the kind of unique situations that would fit under the developers mention of 'occasional exceptions.'<br /> <br /> From the first second edition book, ghosts were said to be Ranked based on their 'self-awareness,' which Integrity covers. And at the cost of 2 Experiences per dot, I wouldn't get hooked on the idea that people's Integrity only goes down and stays there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those rules will affect whole <b>CoD</b> games universe, just like portray of Underworld in <b>Geist </b>1E was made canon and it's fundament for <b>Mage</b> 2E games now. <b>Development process is <i>exactly</i> moment you rise this kind concerns.</b> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld was detailed in a blue book. And you're raising the concern in a general thread to other forum posters, instead of the Geist thread where the remark was mentioned. You're not offering your opinion to the developer, you're trying to get the forum at large to agree with you that he's wrong and you're right, based on one remark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:21:32-08:00","id":1026014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026006#post1026006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 2 ghosts CAN Manifest, so this sentance must mean Rank 1 beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 0 &quot;ghosts&quot; can't Manifest and are the kind of phenomena you keep describing in terms of minor supernatural phenomena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just by sheer numbers - Integrity 7 is norm in mortal society. Rarely there are people with lower Integrity, so most dying people fulfilling 'ghosts needs' will be Integrity 7, it's simply statistic. </div> </div> </div>What makes you think that the circumstances which are likely to form a ghost are equally likely to affect people with the same Integrity as a starting mortal character?<br /> <br /> Desperation is not kind to the dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Recording' types do not plan or avenge their murdered, they just repeat scene of their death, at most. </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;The Ranks of the Dead,&quot; sidebar, MtAw 2e p245</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Manes:</b> Rank 1 ghosts. <u>Most Manes are not truly intelligent, but can speak and act according to patterns complex enough to fake it.</u> When confronted with something beyond their obsessions, their limitations become clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:22:30-08:00","id":1026015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026001#post1026001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice that starting at Rank 2 means starting at a level of cognizance that recognizes not every red-haired man is their murderer and that it won't help to kill false positives, whereas starting at Rank 1 means the potentially-illusory promise of getting there <i>eventually</i> is reason enough for them to be an autonomous territorial serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, so Rank 2 ghosts is proper 'avenging ghost' archtype. Rank 1, beside being literally cold snaps and repetitioners of their death scenes, can still be 'random killing people ghosts'. Great. All supernatural popculture points they are more numerous so Rank 1<i> should </i>be more numerous on rule. And so we return to Integrity 7 ghosts being Rank 1 on general, for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026001#post1026001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Higher Rank is not mutually requisite of higher <i>starting</i> Rank and higher <i>starting</i> Rank generally comes with the good sense not to go poking around under the rock where the dead things live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. Even with proposed guidelines I can make exceptions all day long. I just point that on general rules should make Rank 1 ghosts more numerous and many Rank 2 ghosts as low Integrity from start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026001#post1026001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leave the goalposts where they were unless you have a vast library of ghost fiction whose central supernatural character fulfills their pursuit within the same day.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you do not point to very unlikely scenario just to prove it's doable as something that should be norm in horror setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026001#post1026001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My engaging in a half-meta description of the &quot;thought process&quot; that leads to a ghost with an obsession opting to stay in the Underworld to build their power for a while once banished there upon using the newfound awareness that Rank 2 provides is not a description of a conscious decision to leave its Anchor(s) behind \u2014 it's in keeping with the genre that the peace of the grave permits a fairly rapid return to one's faculties as a ghost who has lost its hold on the land of the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, you just sent our 'vengeful ghosts' that should be going over her oppressors, not too Underworld, where she lose Anchors that would her connect to this hunt in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:28:36-08:00","id":1026021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026015#post1026015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, you just sent our 'vangful ghosts' that should be going over her opresosor to Underworld, where she lose Anchors that would her connect to this hunt in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, going to the Underworld does not cause a ghost to lose the obsessions that relate to their Anchors. The Underworld <i>is where ghosts go when the Anchors their obsessions relate to no longer exist.</i> Burning down the cannibal killer's house will exile him to the Great Below, but it doesn't make him stop being the ghost of a cannibal killer. He'll be back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:35:29-08:00","id":1026031,"title":"","content":"Okay, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, I see that Rank 0 ghosts are all those will-o-wisps and simple Poltergeists. Mea Culpa, point for you. So now all those massive Integrity 7 deaths should go to Rank 0 Plasms, as they should be most numerous in setting. I see that Rank 1 Manes <i>really</i> are more for 'obsessive murderers' if they can work faking humans acts, having obsessions more about it. So lower Integrity for it are okay. But then, where we should put Rank 2? In the table like:<br /> <br /> Integrity 8-9 -&gt; Rank 2<br /> Integrity 7 -&gt; Rank 0<br /> Integrity 6&lt; -&gt; Rank 1 ( killer ghosts? )<br /> <br /> It seems... not elegant. Not to mention devs themselves not pointed to Rank 0 ghosts even existing in guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:52:30-08:00","id":1026043,"title":"","content":"Rank 0 Ghosts aren't ghosts. They are the result of Ghosts doing things and being places, ghosts only of consequence, not of creatures with identity.<br /> <br /> Rank 0 Ghosts are the piss of a ghost peeing against a wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:59:29-08:00","id":1026049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1025917#post1025917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, my biggest crude with those guidelines is this - Rank 2 ghosts should be more violent and low Integrity, Rank 1 ghosts should be more stable - to make the typical 'ghost stories' more probable. Because now, with those guidelines, it looks like you almost do not get <i>any</i> violent Rank 2 ghosts - and those that <i>should</i> be violent are only 'will-o-whisps' and cold spots Rank 1. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Few things to say here.<br /> <br /> 1) Not that the Chronicles world is the real world, but the vast majority of ghost stories people have are of ghosts actually being benign, generally having the worst of their experience just being the surprise of the experience. The Chronicles world does indeed darken that, but that just as often means that these benign ghosts have ways of making themselves known that just happen to be alarming. On that note,<br /> <br /> 2) A vast majority of the violence in ghost stories over the course of years(millenia, really) does not come from a violent, murderous disposition held by the figure in life, but is the result of being trapped with an unresolved fixation. These people are trapped between worlds, nailed there by some passion, a feeling that they can't let go off, a feeling that has not manifested, or has manifested but in a way that does not satisfy. That lack of catharsis, that lack of satisfaction, becomes all consuming, and the corresponding emotional reaction to that is frustration, manic-depressive mood swings, tension, anxiety-all reasons why a person would react violently. Ghosts have the problem of what happens when &quot;If we pretend[read: be <i>x</i>] long enough, never giving up, it just might be who we are&quot; is applied in a circumstances of limited space, infinite time, and a failure of resources create an emotional response that will probably be worn for as long as they fail, as those failures and emotions pile on them like blankets-or more accurately, shrouds.<br /> <br /> We have a fixation on the murderer ghost now because it's a good story both as enjoyment and as cultural training tools, but that's particular stories against the wider backdrop. Speaking of-<br /> <br /> 3) While it's a mistake to assume that equilibrium is the natural state of any ecosystem-it's not, things ebb and flow according to minor devastations at all times with only moments of calm-there is generally a realm of acceptable chaos. Unless you are dealing with slice of life stories (Which I know for a fact you do <i>not</i> do), by and large this realm of &quot;life as acceptable&quot; is not where you tell your stories. You tell them where the equanimity breaks, when something breaches status quo for the characters. If we assume your reading is correct(It's not, though some credit must be given if for no other reason that non-underworld ghosts can have kingdoms too, even if they pale compared to the empires connected to the Below) and that by and large Rank 2 are generally more peaceful than Rank 1 ghosts and also have more power to enact their will to further that peace by subjugating the Manes, that just means it's all the more alarming when a Lemure acts out. They are a clear standing nail to deal with, which is the stuff of stories. The Equanimity is Broken, Fix It. And in relation to that-<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm going to start calling them Manes and Lemures ala Awakening's things, because Rank 1 and Rank 2 is boring and stuffy)<br /> <br /> 4) Obsessive ghosts are well, good, and fine. Many a ghost story is satisfying dealing with a mindless, ravaging ghost. <i>BUT</i> that falls apart a little in longer form stories or games-you often see these more mindlessly aggressive types in what amounts to a one shot. Any longer going story tends towards more intelligent opponents, creatures that can use their power in more precise ways to facilitate designs and plots. Lemures being both more aware of themselves and more powerful while still obsessing over their lives means that the average surface dwelling ghost is, at any given point, a better antagonist for the sort of games people are playing than not. And on that mixture, let's talk about-<br /> <br /> 5) Integrity can more or less translate into &quot;how well you keep yourself together&quot;, as many have pointed out already. That we have not had a high Integrity murderer in a book yet is sort of incidental to the fact that we just haven't had anyone interested in writing a high Integrity murderer in the places where we've had room for it, and that room is pretty sparse to begin with. Anyways, the point is that a High Integrity person keeps themselves together in the face of the traumatic by virtue of their &quot;centeredness&quot;-one way or another, they can keep from breaking by things they do and affirm themselves, while a Low Integrity person is much more prone to patching shit up with outside rituals and actions. These traits invariably give them less personal agency in life, and in death, when your passions and obsessions are the things that keep you from entropy, your willingness to surrender your identity to rituals and forms more or less who you are, but it also means you have little substance-you are literally a less substantial person as someone who is not self-possessive. In a game of ghosts, where substance is power, that means you're the bitch. And there are a lot of people who become the bitches of the world of the dead, because-<br /> <br /> 6) It is faulty to assume that the majority of the people in the world are Integrity 7 upon death. Sure, PC's start that way, and it is assumed to be the baselines for a lot of souls you deal with-but I personally don't find it unrealistic to assume that a lot of people Integrity 6, actually. Oh, sure, the majority aren't terrible, but I think a lot of people get broken in ways and just find small ways to handle it that has nothing to do with actual healing/self-actualizing and or -transcending. You don't have to do bad things to be low-Integrity, or even take a hit, you just have to have things you can't handle, and that happens to a lot of people. It's kind of mundane, how damage of that sort happens. And speaking of mundane-<br /> <br /> 7) There's this odd position that just because Lemures might be more populous than Manes means that the canon is violated because it posits that the terrifying spectres of lore are rare but &quot;how can that be if the current relation between Lemures and Manes indicates that more powerful and narratively violent creatures are more populous, increasing as you go up the scale&quot; which is not only bad statistics and failing to account that Rank 3 upwards often maintain in the Underworld and their presence is definitely an uproar-all of that ignores that Rank 2 <i>anythings</i> are basically the equivalent of beginning PCs. A Lemure is nowhere near the rank &quot;Legendary and Terrifying Spectres of Lore&quot;. Don't blow it out of proportion.<br /> <br /> So, no, things are as it should be. The only cause of disquiet is your own handling of the affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:25:04-08:00","id":1026066,"title":"","content":"While I don't disagree with what you wrote, I'm not sure how to adapt this to the Guardian/Seer tactic of torturing your victim into Ghost-hood so you can plunder their memories and personalities for loot. I liked the idea of grinding targets Integrity to 0 and creating a large breaking point density to ensure the Ghost-aization. :&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:33:14-08:00","id":1026074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026006#post1026006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot say how much you must miss reading <b>CoD corebook</b> to assume that Rank 2 should be more numerous:</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) Prove it. 2) My personal take is &quot;there is exactly as many Rank 1 or Rank 2 ghosts as necessary for individual stories.&quot; Some stories will have more Rank 2 than Rank 1, some will have equal, some will do same as you say. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rank 2 ghosts CAN Manifest, so this sentance must mean Rank 1 beings. </div> </div> </div> What stops Rank 1 ghosts? All you need is Influence 1 to make an appropriate Condition to manifest.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just by sheer numbers </div> </div> </div> Your numbers, which aren't universal across all tables. 7 can be considered an average, so its not too much for another table to assume that means that we have roughly equal number of people above and below 7. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant 'vengeful torture victim', like, you know, many of 'they were tortured by life and now are after her oppressors or their decedents'. This kind persons are having rather lower Integrity - and should be rather more cognitive than simple 'will-o-wisps' Rank 1 ghosts are. </div> </div> </div> 1) First of all, I disagree with your overgeneralization. Victims are not some universal statistic. They're individuals who react differently to different environments. Secondly, Rank 1 are still capable beings, though of limited mentality. Third, not all torture victims will have low Integrity - a number of real life torture victims come out mentally stronger, and all you need is one of those people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just see over Intimidation use on Violent Skills from <b>Hurt Locker</b>: </div> </div> </div> I have, but breaking points are not an absolute that you're treating them as. The point of torture is to break someone. It doesn't always work. Especially not in the type of stories you are refering to in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Recording' types do not plan or avenge their murdered, they just repeat scene of their death, at most. </div> </div> </div> Nope. They can totally react to intruders or someone that triggers memories of their death. That's all you deciding what rank 1 can or cannot do. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see rather your augmentations as full of holes and trying to stretch things to work with 'devs initial idea'. </div> </div> </div> *shrugs* My only argument is that you are mistaking your view of the CofD with what's official, and what others can interpret the game as. You've confused how things work officially versus in your game, and are now spreading misinformation based on that misunderstanding. <br /> <br /> You want to run things that way, more power to you. But you are mistaken if you think your view is universal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:45:55-08:00","id":1026085,"title":"","content":"Most of my problem comes from <b>CoD Rulebook</b> not mentioning that:<br /> A. Rank 0 ghosts are those 'cold spots', Will-o-Whisps and guys just staying dead after accident.<br /> AND<br /> B. Rank 1 ghosts working more or less human, just obsessive, and automatic in secret.<br /> <br /> I simply missed that in <b>Mage</b> 2E there are described <i>11 ghosts Ranks</i>, in reality. If you move everything on one Rank from this that are described in <b>CoD Rulebook</b>, <u><i>everything</i></u> starts to make sense. ( Cause low Integrity Rank 1 ghosts that ARE obsessive killers is working with mine previous murderers and avenging tortures victims ). Rank 2, as totally self-aware ghosts, being like PCs in universe are okay with that assumptions on hierarchy. Just embroiled lore arrangement between books ( <b>CoD Rulebook</b> and <b>Mage</b> 2E ) obscured everything.<br /> <br /> There is still a bit problem for me on power-wise scale, with Rank 2 granting you much more Numina and Attributes. But if our previous Rank 1 'auto repeating terminator' ghost can become Rank 2 in the way of his 'unlife' evolution on Earth ( without jumping to Underworld ), I think I'm more or less okay with this spread.<br /> <br /> Jarring is also this 'Rank 0 is not in guidelines', so we do not have any hints where our cold spots or Will-o-Wisp <i>will</i> show up, beyond - 'whenever you like them'. Not every dead become Rank 0 ghost, only small percent of them will, and some points of it will solve also this smaller problem.<br /> <br /> Also, question on examples - classical <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poltergeist\" target=\"_blank\">Poltergeist ghost</a> - Rank 0, Rank 1 or Rank 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:50:37-08:00","id":1026091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026066#post1026066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't disagree with what you wrote, I'm not sure how to adapt this to the Guardian/Seer tactic of torturing your victim into Ghost-hood so you can plunder their memories and personalities for loot. I liked the idea of grinding targets Integrity to 0 and creating a large breaking point density to ensure the Ghost-aization. :&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand new shown facts, Rank 1 'repetitive terminators' ARE having memories and personalities of their originals. They are just fixated on solving 'unfinished business' and cannot make other decisions. Still, they can tell you what you need if they will be convinced they will resolve their businesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:06:14-08:00","id":1026096,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I <i>think</i> Rank 1 Ghosts are closer in mentality (if not power) to Agatha Hagglethorn (Dresden Files, Grave Peril), in that they interpret everything within the context of their &quot;haunting&quot;. Kravos (same book) would be closer to a Rank 2 in mentality - able to adapt and understand things outside their &quot;business&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:33:52-08:00","id":1026113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026096#post1026096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I <i>think</i> Rank 1 Ghosts are closer in mentality (if not power) to Agatha Hagglethorn (Dresden Files, Grave Peril), in that they interpret everything within the context of their &quot;haunting&quot;. Kravos (same book) would be closer to a Rank 2 in mentality - able to adapt and understand things outside their &quot;business&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>exactly</i> what I though on big reveal of Rank 0 ghosts being a thing. Still, you can make Agatha to tell all you need to know, as she <b>has</b> memories of her life - you only need to 'play by her ideas', and maybe purpose to give her something related to her 'business' for her to open.<br /> <br /> Still, torturing/questioning Rank 1 ghosts for information is still viable tactics then, as they have their previous bodies memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:12:30-08:00","id":1026131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026113#post1026113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, torturing/questioning Rank 1 ghosts for information is still viable tactics then, as they have their previous bodies memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are essentially a personality/identity fork off the original - of course they have the prior body's memories. Except when they don't. No one said their memories are <i>accurate</i>. After all, living people misremember things all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:27:18-08:00","id":1026139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026131#post1026131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are essentially a personality/identity fork off the original - of course they have the prior body's memories. Except when they don't. No one said their memories are <i>accurate</i>. After all, living people misremember things all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind what happens when they get hooked up to powers of entropy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:28:35-08:00","id":1026140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026139#post1026139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevermind what happens when they get hooked up to powers of entropy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that voids their warranty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:45:52-08:00","id":1026217,"title":"","content":"Well, a lot sure happened while I was asleep. Looks like I'm the only one whose UTC is off.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it looks like the issue of Plasms and Manes and Lemures have been largely solved in my absence, so I add another question on the subject of ghosts and their Integrity.<br /> The rules for ghosts indicate that while their Integrity rating is fixed, it becomes 'fluid' again when they become self-cognizant again. What circumstances would cause that? Is rising to Lemure-hood enough, or is there something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:29:28-08:00","id":1026241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026217#post1026217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for ghosts indicate that while their Integrity rating is fixed, it becomes 'fluid' again when they become self-cognizant again. What circumstances would cause that? Is rising to Lemure-hood enough, or is there something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling &quot;All Lares are aware that they're no longer living&quot; is relevant \u2014 actually grasping that you're dead and/or not the person you remember being might serve as a decent basis.<br /> <br /> Then again, Mage's version of the ghost rules just says that ghosts don't suffer breaking points at all and Create Ghost makes no reference to the Integrity rating of its eponymous product, so this could be a case of old iterations of the mechanics sticking around.<br /> <br /> Then again again, Mage's version of the ghost rules also doesn't include the memory-based means of gaining Essence, so the above could just be a matter of wordcount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:41:22-08:00","id":1026339,"title":"","content":"I want to return to my main concerns in below shown questions and would be very pleased if someone could help me with those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026085#post1026085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is still a bit problem for me on power-wise scale, with Rank 2 granting you much more Numina and Attributes. But if our previous Rank 1 'auto repeating terminator' ghost can become Rank 2 in the way of his 'unlife' evolution on Earth ( without jumping to Underworld ), I think I'm more or less okay with this spread.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Can Manes ( Rank 1) ghost become Lemures ( Rank 2 ) on his own? <i>Without</i> going to Underworld? </b>Like, I don't know, solving some Anchors, maybe?<br /> <br /> And returning to better grasping the idea - How this difference system works on classical example.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026085#post1026085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, question on examples - classical <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poltergeist\" target=\"_blank\">Poltergeist ghost</a> - Rank 0, Rank 1 or Rank 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will Poltergeist by Rank 1 or Rank 2 ghosts? ( I really do not think he will be simply Rank 0 ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:13:34-08:00","id":1026349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026339#post1026339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to return to my main concerns in below shown questions and would be very pleased if someone could help me with those.<br /> <br /> <b>Can Manes ( Rank 1) ghost become Lemures ( Rank 2 ) on his own? <i>Without</i> going to Underworld? </b>Like, I don't know, solving some Anchors, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by RAW, but there's no reason it couldn't in your home games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026339#post1026339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And returning to better grasping the idea - How this difference system works on classical example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026339#post1026339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Poltergeist by Rank 1 or Rank 2 ghosts? ( I really do not think he will be simply Rank 0 ).</div> </div> </div> </div>A Poltergeist is just a haunting characterized by objects moving on their own, often violently, and usually attached to a person rather than a place. So any ghost of Rank 1 or greater could theoretically be a Poltergeist, all they need is the Fetter Manifestation and the Telekinesis Numen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:16:15-08:00","id":1026350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026349#post1026349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not by RAW, but there's no reason it couldn't in your home games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any idea on what needed circumstances for rising from Rank 1 to Rank 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T05:49:30-08:00","id":1026463,"title":"","content":"Are you asking for potential houseruling or by RAW? 'Cause there's only the Underworld and Death Mages that can up ghost Ranks by RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:09:47-08:00","id":1026485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025758-2e-ghosts-integrity-how-to-get-your-rank?p=1026463#post1026463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you asking for potential houseruling or by RAW? 'Cause there's only the Underworld and Death Mages that can up ghost Ranks by RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's even go in to possible house ruling, as by RAW I doubt any dev will look over this problem. What could you think that Rank 1 ghost do to become Rank 2 ( without above stated solutions )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:29:53-08:00","id":1026502,"title":"","content":"In that case I'd have ghosts that are active (use Manifestations, Numina, boost their attributes) get more powerful. Ghosts that haunts remote places or lack the powers to actually act will stay the same, but a ghost that has the chance of acting out and does so will get the &quot;exercise&quot; necessary to grow. This would also require getting more Essence than most other ghosts so such ghosts would require being highly remembered (perhaps as a local legend) unless they're fed Essence by someone else or has a rare Numen that allows them to gain Essence from other sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:05:05-08:00","id":1026679,"title":"","content":"I've personally been tinkering with the idea of ghosts potentially growing in Rank (at least from 1 to 2) through a combination of age, activity, and relative noteriety. So, say, a formerly-weak Mane haunting a particular road as a &quot;phantom hitchhiker&quot; might eventually grow into a Lemure over time if their tale - not just any phantom hitchhiker story, but specifically &quot;The Vanishing Passenger of Old Lake Road&quot; or what-have-you - gets told often enough, for long enough, and enough people have encounters with them. It could (and probably should) take years or even decades for them to grow this way, though.<br /> <br /> Granted, this is a bit of a shift from the main rules, since ghosts are usually &quot;fed&quot; through being remembered as they were when they were <i>alive</i>. Not to mention, there should probably be drawbacks to growth through being more-or-less &quot;anchored&quot; to their tale, like being <i>shaped</i> by it as well... which starts to blur the line between ghosts and other ephemeral beings, but hey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:44:35-08:00","id":1026781,"title":"","content":"I was thinking something in the lines of devouring other ghosts to rise in Rank, or merging into one entity after forming a hive-mind of some sort thanks to a shared haunting spot. Got that idea from Specters in Wraith the Oblivion, and Hollows from Bleach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:44:45-08:00","id":1027262,"title":"","content":"I like your thinking there too. There <i>is</i> precedent in the core for ephemerals feeding off others of the same kind already, so why not let a particularly desperate or callous ghost take it a step further in a manner echoing Diablerie, the Shadow's food chain as a whole, and the like? Hell, I'd personally be tempted to let them <i>eventually</i> go beyond Rank 2 if they pursued that method... though they might start looking less like a ghost, or at least their original self, at that point, in much the same way other entities suffer from feeding &quot;the wrong way&quot; from their own kind. Could even slap a weird form of psychic vampirism on them that converts to essence instead if you want them to also feed off the living, in a more effective and complete manner than the Drain Numen permits...<br /> <br /> Maybe there's even room for multiple forms of &quot;evolution&quot; among ghosts in a single setting, each with its own perks and drawbacks. Ghostly &quot;templates&quot;, if you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 01-05-2017, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}